Maybe CSS parent height? Not. Could be a browser issue with SVG? Use JS events. Let's adjust script to use attached and evaluate. Also results `.music-card` maybe not visible but DOM. We'll use count. For form, use evaluate.

Need wait for catalog 6; count. Then set input via `evaluate` and dispatch `input`; then submit form by calling `angular.element(form).triggerHandler('submit')`? Since Angular's `ngSubmit` uses `$event` and maybe triggering DOM submit event works. We can use:
```
page.evaluate("""
() => {
 const input = document.querySelector('input[ng-model="Sequencia.novaSequencia"]');
 const setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype,'value').set;
 setter.call(input,'bm,e');
 input.dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true}));
 const form = document.querySelector('.sequencia-form form');
 form.dispatchEvent(new Event('submit',{bubbles:true,cancelable:true}));
}
""")
```
Angular ngModel listens input event; should update. Angular form ngSubmit listens submit. Good.
